#
# A311D SYSTEM-level default for the front-end service list.
#
# /usr/bin/autostart ends with "systemctl start ${UI_SERVICE}". Without a
# value here (or in /storage/.config/profile.d) systemd is invoked with no
# unit name and refuses to start anything:
#   systemctl[1695]: Too few arguments.
#
# A311D needs sway (Wayland compositor) first and EmulationStation (essway)
# on top of it. Starting essway alone leaves the front-end without an EGL
# display. rocknix-autostart.service runs bash with "source /etc/profile",
# and /usr/bin/autostart re-sources /etc/profile just before starting the
# UI, so a value in this directory is picked up on every boot.
#
# /etc/profile sources /etc/profile.d/* BEFORE /storage/.config/profile.d/*,
# so the matching platform quirk (quirks/platforms/A311D/090-ui_service)
# writes the same value into /storage as a user-layer fallback.
UI_SERVICE="sway.service essway.service"
